What:		/sys/devices/platform/.../gpu_power_ceiling
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Asahi Linux contributors <asahi@lists.linux.dev>
Description:
		Read-only. Present when the GPU's device-tree node is a
		cooling device (#cooling-cells). One key/value pair per line:

		requested_state: thermal cooling state, 0..100.
		requested_ceiling_mw: minimum of all requester ceilings.
		applied_ceiling_mw: ceiling last written to the firmware.
		provisional_floor_mw: lowest ceiling, 25 percent of the
		initialized maximum (never zero).
		achieved_ceiling_mw: always "unsupported"; the firmware does
		not acknowledge the ceiling.

		State N requests max(25, 100 - N) percent of the initialized
		maximum power. The debugfs file asahi-<device>-power/ceiling
		adds the read-back firmware words and each requester's ceiling.
